{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the men were grieved and burned with anger.</b> The grief was because <b>a vile thing had been done in Israel</b> — it was a disgrace among Israel, even though among the Canaanites it was not so — and because it was unprecedented then to force the daughters of the great men of the generation, as it says, <b>so let it not be done</b>. Therefore they were angered that such a thing had been done against them."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:12.997360822Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}